<% content_for :title, "Terms of Service" %>
<div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-3xl px-4 py-14 md:px-8">
  <p class="text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-algae-900 dark:text-algae-300">Terms of Service</p>
  <h1 class="mt-2 font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">The short, honest version first.</h1>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-[#8a938d] dark:text-fog">Effective October 5, 2026. Plain language first; counsel reviews before paid plans launch. By creating an account you agree to these terms.</p>

  <div class="mt-8 space-y-8 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#3d4742] dark:text-clay">
    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-[#1c2420] dark:text-ink">The service</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">Trellixe provides shared outreach lists for church teams: contacts, events, invitations, follow-ups, todos, and timelines. We may improve, modify, or discontinue parts of the service; material changes are announced in-app first. Uptime is a goal, not a guarantee.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-[#1c2420] dark:text-ink">Your account and your authority</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">You must provide a working email and keep your password private. Crucially: churches enter <span class="font-semibold">other people's</span> personal details — names, numbers, prayer requests, including minors. By doing so you warrant that you have the authority to share them (your church's mandate, parental or guardian consent where required) and that you will honor access, export, and deletion requests for that data as described in our <%= link_to "Privacy Policy", privacy_path, class: "font-semibold text-algae-900 underline hover:text-algae-700 dark:text-algae-300" %>.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-[#1c2420] dark:text-ink">Acceptable use</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">Use Trellixe for genuine outreach work. Do not spam, harass, or message people who asked to be left alone; do not enter unlawful content; do not scrape, probe, or access other workspaces' data; do not resell access or misrepresent the service. We may suspend workspaces that breach this, after warning where practical.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-[#1c2420] dark:text-ink">Workspaces, roles, and seats</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">Each workspace has member and admin roles with the permissions shown in-app. Free workspaces are limited to five members. Workspace admins are responsible for their members' conduct and for removing people who leave the team — removal ends access immediately.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-[#1c2420] dark:text-ink">Payments (when paid plans launch)</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">Paid plans will bill per branch or per seat as shown on the pricing page at purchase, in advance, with receipts for every charge. Non-payment suspends paid features after notice — your data is retained for 90 days so you can export or resume. No refunds for partial periods unless the law where you live requires otherwise.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-[#1c2420] dark:text-ink">Your data, leaving, and termination</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">Your workspace data is yours: export or delete it any time from inside the app. Delete a workspace and its data follows, with backups aging out within 30 days. We may terminate accounts that breach these terms; you may leave any time by deleting your workspaces. Termination ends access, never our duty to delete on request.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-[#1c2420] dark:text-ink">Liability and warranty</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">Trellixe is provided "as is" for organizing outreach work; it is not a substitute for pastoral, legal, or professional judgment. To the maximum extent permitted by law, our liability is limited to amounts you paid in the preceding twelve months (zero on free plans). Nothing here limits rights the law does not allow limiting.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-[#1c2420] dark:text-ink">Changes and contact</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">Material changes take effect after in-app notice; continued use means acceptance. For the contracting entity, governing law, and anything else: write to us from the contact page — a human replies, and counsel localizes this document before paid plans launch.</p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <%= link_to "Back home", root_path, class: "mt-10 inline-flex rounded-lg border border-[#D9DDE0] bg-white px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold hover:border-algae-300 dark:bg-card dark:border-white/10" %>
</div>
